+# Continuity / follow-up: a9987d0 salvage audit
+
+## Entry point for the next agent
+
+Read [the audit and its scope limits](AUDIT-a9987d0-2026-10-11.md) before using
+any code from the incoming consolidation. Baseline for this patch series:
+`106b7e357133e7bb856836d903731b98c7da0a66`; incoming commit:
+`a9987d0e8e97db148dbf91bf307b72a93357eb60`.
+
+**Do not replay or cherry-pick the full incoming commit.** It is a different
+repository state, not a reviewed incremental improvement to this fork.
+
+## Accomplished
+
+- Inventoried all 223 changed paths against committed baseline entries, including
+  deletions and file modes. Added reproducible `--commit` inventory mode to the
+  existing audit tool instead of another parallel oracle framework.
+- Reproduced a current-fork SWAR miscompile with a reduced C function: narrowing
+  intermediate stages returned full-width popcounts. Added Copy-only structural
+  traversal, per-node width checks, and value-preserving shared-input checks.
+- Red-teamed the repair rather than stopping at its first passing test: found a
+  separate CLZ select-stage truncation miscompile (`31` expected, `30` returned).
+  Fixed the shared select traversal and added CLZ/CTZ positive/negative controls.
+- The canonical CLZ control then exposed the defined zero-result bug (32
+  instead of 31). Fixed lowering with the proved `Clz(x | 1)` identity, deferred
+  reverse-order insertion, source-span maintenance, and a two-network
+  pass-level/idempotence test. CTZ zero remains 63 as required.
+- Added targeted Rust contract tests and deterministic C tests with independently
+  computed expectations. The SWAR C test demonstrably fails the pre-fix compiler;
+  the CLZ C test fails the first-fix-only compiler.
+- Salvaged both missing SQLite-derived reduced regressions; added noinline,
+  independent expectations, exhaustive byte-pair coverage, zero-length/zero-trip
+  and partial-trimming cases, and meaningful nonzero failure exits.
+- Added a bounded, fail-closed fast gate to both local and hosted CI. A failed
+  runtime/timeout prints the test/optimization level and its diagnostic output.
+- Executed GCC ASan+UBSan on the four C tests.
+- Used the existing strict workload runner for gzip, zlib-ng, Expat, SQLite,
+  Linux find-bit and glibc memcmp extracts. Before/after output parity and binary
+  identities are recorded; this is not a claim to have built their whole parent
+  projects.
+- Used the existing Compiler Explorer oracle against GCC 16.2, Clang 23.1.0,
+  ICC 2021.10.0 and ICX latest. Assembly and counts retained. No hardware timing
+  or PMU-derived superiority claim.
+- Reviewed linker version preferences: existing bfd 2.47 / mold 2.42.1 and
+  `MOLD_TARGETS='X86_64;I386'` already satisfy the requested build selectors.
+  Existing version-guard test passes. No linker patch is justified here.
+- Installed and activated 6 GiB of swap on the largest writable filesystem.
+  All compiler builds use fastbuild at O1 with two Cargo jobs.
+- Used the repository's hardened descendant of the requested snapshot script:
+  atomic patch, bounded compressed checkpoints, tracked-source tarball, session
+  bundle with explicit base prerequisite, verified ZIP and restoration receipt.
+  Intermediate validated fixes are saved immediately as explicitly UNGATED
+  checkpoints while the complete fast mirror is pending. Only a matching final
+  fast CI stamp qualifies the final publication.
+
+The final gate result belongs to the exact-tree CI log/receipt, not an assumption
+in this document. Do not infer full/slow CI from a fast stamp.
+
+## Prioritized remaining research, with acceptance requirements
+
+| Priority | Work | Evidence / hypothesis | Required acceptance proof |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| P1 | Nonzero-aware CLZ guard elimination | Final red-team assembly of existing `bitops.c` shows an extra `movq` + `orq $1` before `lzcntl`, even though its source already guards zero. The six byte-identical workload kernels do not cover this cost. | Reuse a dominating-nonzero/range proof to omit OR only where safe; keep all new zero/cast regressions and positive controls. Output-check the benchmark before a quiescent paired timing comparison. Do not weaken the zero-case fix or claim a runtime regression from static counts alone. |
+| P1 | Return-register coalescing for scalar bit intrinsics | Canonical SWAR becomes `popcnt input,temp; mov temp,eax; ret` (3 instructions), versus Clang's 2. | Reproducer with multiple uses, narrow returns and ABI constraints; register/liveness proof; unchanged correctness; target assembly delta; matched runtime experiment on real hardware before a speed claim. |
+| P1 | Safe truncated SWAR recognition | `swar_low16` is now correct at 18 static instructions, best oracle 16. A proved rewrite to popcount of a masked input could be much shorter. | Prove each accepted mask/cast stage separately. Exhaustive narrow-domain and randomized full-width tests, shared-user tests, all-target capability gates, ISA-disabled fallback, and independent reference. Do not reinstate generic cast peeling. |
+| P1 | Wider bit-idiom structural audit | This session found two distinct structural traversals ignoring casts despite earlier identity fixes. | Systematically mutate internal widths, casts and operand sharing in CLZ/CTZ/bswap/rotate matchers. Focus on meaningful, defined C reproducers and cheap IR tests; no unbounded fuzz campaign. The retained count-zero test covers the demonstrated CLZ issue; no CTZ miscompile was demonstrated here. |
+| P2 | Complete semantic adjudication of the 151 diverged incoming paths | Exact entry comparison cannot prove adoption/soundness. Large vectorizer/RA/peephole deltas are not independently approved by this audit. | Select only genuinely new behaviors, identify changed legality contracts, minimal failing case first. Keep current fork protections. Reject unmeasured rewrites. |
+| P2 | Current SQLite integration breadth | Incoming multi-table workload has useful transactions/joins/index ideas but unsafe binding lifetime and unchecked API returns. | Integrate only missing scenarios into the existing pinned SQLite workload, use SQLITE_TRANSIENT for temporary strings or clear bindings while alive, check every API result, fingerprint cached objects, and run project-level differential validation in an explicitly authorized workload session. |
+| P3 | Phi anti-dependence splitting | Incoming prototype has stale instruction coordinates and missing span maintenance; reported Mandelbrot gain is not a local measurement. | Prototype outside the active pipeline. Two recurrences sharing a block, loop nesting, terminator-only uses, generic value replacement and span validation. Compare current allocator first; no new pass unless measurable benefit remains. |
+| P3 | MachInst allocator | Incoming allocator/rewrite functions have no callers; spills and clobber modeling are incomplete. | Do not import dead code. If revisited, wire a minimal isolated instruction set, verify call/div fixed intervals, multi-spill legalization and absence of virtual-register leakage, then compare against current allocator on real pressure-heavy kernels. |
+
+These are research candidates, not promised gains and not hidden failures of the
+submitted fixes. This audit does not certify superiority over other compilers,
+full-kernel behavior, or the entire incoming source tree.
+
+## Efficient validation recipes
+
+```sh
+# Two-job O1 compiler build; explicit memory knobs also keep CI at -j2.
+CARGO_PROFILE_FASTBUILD_DEBUG=0 CARGO_INCREMENTAL=0 scripts/build_lccc_fast.sh
+
+# Cheap targeted contract (also wired into --fast CI).
+CCC=target/fastbuild/lccc bash tests/regression/check_a9987_salvage.sh
+
+# Six representative extracted workloads, exact output checks, no noisy timing.
+python3 tests/benchmark/run_benchmarks.py \
+  --only gzip_crc32,zlib_ng_adler32,expat_xml_scan,sqlite_varint,linux_find_bit,glibc_memcmp \
+  --compilers lccc,gcc --opt=-O2 --skip-perf --strict \
+  --artifact-dir target/a9987-workloads --json target/a9987-workloads.json
+
+# The publication gate; no slow gates in this audit.
+CARGO_PROFILE_FASTBUILD_DEBUG=0 CARGO_INCREMENTAL=0 CI_LOCAL_JOBS=2 \
+  bash scripts/ci_local.sh --fast
+
+# Published codegen comparison: static counts, NOT a performance benchmark.
+python3 scripts/codegen_oracle.py tests/regression/swar_intermediate_casts.c \
+  --function swar_full --function swar_low16 --local target/fastbuild/lccc \
+  --flags '-O2 -march=x86-64-v3' --oracles gcc16.2,clang,icc,icx \
+  --artifact-dir target/a9987-oracle --json target/a9987-oracle.json
+```
+
+Never compare the old wrong `swar_low16` against the corrected scalar code as a
+performance baseline. For VM screening, prefer exact machine-code identity to
+wall-clock noise when the question is non-regression. For actual speedups use
+paired randomized runs, predeclared inputs and stopping rules, confidence
+intervals, separate P/E-core affinity, and hardware counters where available.
+No fabricated PMU substitutes.
+
+## Wipe recovery and final publication
+
+The delivery workspace contains `ms178-1.patch`, its verified ZIP, a full
+tracked-source tarball and recovery script/receipts. Scratch/toolchains may be
+absent next session. Do not depend on symlinks into `/home/lccc-work` surviving.
+The source archive is independently recoverable; the compact session bundle
+requires its explicitly recorded upstream base.
+
+1. Recover using the delivered `LCCC-RECOVER.py` instructions/receipt, or extract
+   the source archive into disposable scratch. Inspect archive metadata first.
+2. Fetch current `ms178/lccc` main, inspect its SHA, and rebase the session commits
+   (or apply the patch to its recorded base before rebasing). Never change
+   `artifacts/.base_ref` without actually reconciling the code.
+3. Install current stable Rust, recreate swap via `scripts/ensure_swap.sh`, and
+   select fastbuild/O1/j2. Toolchain caches are not deliverables.
+4. Run the targeted gate, then `ci_local.sh --fast` on the exact final tree.
+5. Immediately call `scripts/lccc-snapshot.sh` for each validated fix. Its guarded
+   final mode requires the matching tree stamp; an emergency UNGATED save must
+   remain explicitly labeled as such.
+6. Check `git diff --check`, executable modes, patch applicability against the
+   recorded base, ZIP/hash consistency and the source archive's tracked-tree
+   restore proof. Preserve logs and the ledger, not compiler binaries or caches.
+
+The repository publisher counts all workspace files, including excluded caches,
+against its smaller delivery budget. During this session the first publication
+attempt hit that guard; moving scratch/toolchains to the same large root
+filesystem outside the delivery workspace solved it without weakening the guard
+or deleting source. Final archives keep the delivered source independent of
+scratch survival.
